Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from SMPTE
RDD 36:2022, "Apple ProRes Bitstream Syntax and Decoding Process", the
registered disclosure document Apple contributed to SMPTE, which SMPTE
publishes free of charge (https://pub.smpte.org/doc/rdd36/). They are not
translations of, and do not derive from, any other ProRes encoder's or
decoder's source: no other implementation's code was read or consulted, and
none was run to make or check anything here. The tables (codebook choices,
scan orders, quantiser scale) are reproduced from RDD 36. The encoder's
target bit rates are Apple's published figures for each profile.

The tests check the decoder against frames assembled by hand from RDD 36's
syntax tables, the encoder and decoder against each other, and, optionally,
the decoder against frames Apple's encoder wrote: Probe.dev's public sample
AppleProRes422.mov, which is fetched by CI and not included here.

